  "principal_contract": "Complete correctness and exhaustion arguments, the corrected graph-isomorphism criterion, all twelve benchmark rows with the H3 qualification, the four new alternating classifications, the complete Co3 classification and exact verification of all twelve original Hartley--Hulpke auxiliary lists.",
  "literal_theorem_sets_equivalent": false,
  "all_original_assertions_claimed": false,
  "explicit_corrections": [
    {
      "id": "COMPATIBLE_ACTION",
      "source": "Theorem 4.1, physical pages 5--7",
      "correction": "Graph isomorphism detects the automorphisms induced by the normalizer of the chosen faithful permutation action. It detects every abstract automorphism exactly when that normalizer acts surjectively on Aut(G), equivalently when the multiplicities of conjugacy classes of point stabilizers are invariant under Aut(G). Two unrelated embeddings of G and Aut(G) in the same symmetric group do not suffice.",
      "witness": "The accepted degree-six Klein-four example interchanges an involution with one transposition and an involution with two transpositions; the marked groups are abstractly isomorphic but the coloured graphs are not.",
      "component": "compatible_actions"
    },
    {
      "id": "H3_DISCONNECTED",
      "source": "Benchmark table, physical page 4",
      "correction": "For H3 = A5 x C2 there are eleven classes after identifying duals when disconnected diagrams are admitted: eight connected rank-three classes and three disconnected rank-four classes. The printed eight is exactly the connected subfamily.",
      "component": "remaining_censuses + complete acquired H3 proof"
    }
  ],
